module

public import StacksFrontier.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorPower.BaseChange
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Quotient

/-!
# Exterior powers of a reduction modulo an ideal

Let `M` be a module over a commutative ring `R` and let `I` be an ideal of `R`. Reducing the
`n`-th exterior power of `M` modulo `I` gives the `n`-th exterior power, over `R ⧸ I`, of the
reduction of `M`:

`(⋀^n_R M) ⧸ I · ⋀^n_R M  ≃  ⋀^n_{R ⧸ I} ((R ⧸ I) ⊗_R M)`.

This is the special case of base change of exterior powers along the quotient map `R → R ⧸ I`,
and it is the identification of the quotient term in the residue sequence of Stacks 0FMW: there
`I` is generated by a local equation of the divisor, `R ⧸ I` is the structure sheaf of the
divisor, and the right-hand side is `Ω^n` of the divisor.

## Main results

* `exteriorPower.quotSmulTopEquiv`: the equivalence above.

## Implementation notes

Both halves already exist and this file only composes them, which is why it is short. The
exterior power of a base change is `ExteriorAlgebra.exteriorPowerBaseChange`, which holds for an
arbitrary commutative algebra with no flatness hypothesis; the identification of `(R ⧸ I) ⊗_R N`
with `N ⧸ I · N` is `TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul`.

The reduction of `M` is written as `(R ⧸ I) ⊗_R M` rather than as `M ⧸ I • ⊤`. The two are
isomorphic, by the second equivalence above, but only the tensor product carries a `R ⧸ I`-module
structure by instance, and the exterior power on the right has to be taken over `R ⧸ I` — over
`R` it would be a different module, and not the one the divisor's de Rham complex is built from.

The composite is stated as an `R`-linear equivalence. The right-hand side is a `R ⧸ I`-module and
the comparison respects that, but the left-hand side is presented as a quotient of an `R`-module,
so `R`-linearity is the common ground; `restrictScalars` records the step.
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace exteriorPower

universe u v

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]

/-- **Base change of exterior powers along a quotient.** Reducing the `n`-th exterior power of
`M` modulo `I` gives the `n`-th exterior power, over `R ⧸ I`, of the reduction of `M`. -/
noncomputable def quotSmulTopEquiv (I : Ideal R) (n : ℕ) :
    ((⋀[R]^n M) ⧸ (I • (⊤ : Submodule R (⋀[R]^n M)))) ≃ₗ[R]
      ⋀[R ⧸ I]^n ((R ⧸ I) ⊗[R] M) :=
  (TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul (⋀[R]^n M) I).symm.trans
    ((ExteriorAlgebra.exteriorPowerBaseChange R (R ⧸ I) M n).restrictScalars R)

end exteriorPower

end
